    "type": "verse",
    "number": 49,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "The Kinsman-Redeemer. The word goel is used to indicate both the redemption-- \"to free by paying,\" and the Redeemer--\"the one who pays.\" The case of Ruth and Boaz Ruth 2:1; 3:10-18; 4:1-10 perfectly illustrates this beautiful type of Christ. See \"Redemption, (See Scofield \"Isaiah 59:20\").\n\nredeem -- Heb. \"goel,\" Redemp. (Kinsman type).\n\n(See Scofield \"Isaiah 59:20\")."
     }
    ]
